{
  "policy": {
    "scale": 7,
    "mode": "half_even",
    "display_dp": 2,
    "allocation": "largest_remainder"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Shared cross-language test vectors for the stroop-integer money kernel (issue #432).",
    "Consumed by scripts/money-parity.ts, which replays every `input` through both contracts/money",
    "(via `cargo run -p money --example parity_report`) and backend/src/money/decimal.ts, and fails",
    "the build if either side's output differs from `expected` or from the other.",
    "The `round_div` and `split_pro_rata` cases cover the surface both layers genuinely implement in",
    "common. backend/src/money/calculations.ts is float-based and is deliberately out of scope; see",
    "the PR description for why a float comparison would be comparing two different formulas.",
    "The `compute_fee`, `calculate_interest` and `round_amount` cases are the integer reductions of",
    "those operations over the shared kernel -- round_div(principal * rate_bps, 10_000),",
    "round_div(principal * rate_bps * days, 10_000 * 365) and round_div(stroops, 10^5) * 10^5, all",
    "half-even -- so the multiply-then-divide composition and the contract's checked-i128 guards are",
    "exercised without inventing a second production API next to the kernel.",
    "`expected` values come from the kernel harness and are additionally asserted by the",
    "definition-based property checks in contracts/money/tests/parity_vectors.rs and",
    "backend/src/money/__tests__/parity-vectors.test.ts. Empty weight lists cannot be encoded in the",
    "case format (`split_pro_rata:0:`) and are covered by the unit tests in both layers instead."
  ],
